From a10b19e093003b4e38d99db7ac0f3d197d7650bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StonkGuy <68372320+StonkGuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:10:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] rutabaga_gfx(macos): wmtr context type for remoted DXMT
 winemetal calls

A virtio-gpu context type (capset 30) whose guest process forwards DXMT's
winemetal unix calls through a shared-memory ring to a host executor
(libwmtr_host.dylib, loaded with dlopen) that runs them against Metal.
Blobs are POSIX shared memory mapped into the guest by the existing SHM
blob path and into the VMM for the executor; EXECBUFFER carries RING,
KICK and WAIT; WAIT fences complete when the reply slot reaches its
sequence number. The component exists only with STEAMAC_WMTR=1 and a
loadable library, so other guests see no change. The device's
num_capsets counts it then (the stock value 5 covers only virgl, virgl2,
venus, drm and cross-domain, so the guest would never query index 5);
both sides read one cached load of the library.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
